<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to offer HUF 4 bln of 5-yr bonds April 24.</title>
<headline>Hungary to offer HUF 4 bln of 5-yr bonds April 24.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction four billion forints worth of five-year government bonds of the 2001/C series on April 24, the Government Debt Management Agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>BONDS OF THE 2001/C SERIES</p>
<p>    First day of interest		     3 February 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity			   12 December 2001</p>
<p>    Total on offer			     4,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum price				   97.62 pct</p>
<p>Average price at last five-year</p>
<p>     bond auction (March 27)		    99.11 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum yield				   16.35 pct</p>
<p>Average yield at last five-year</p>
<p>     bond auction (March 27)		    15.85 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 15.00 percent, payable semi-annually starting June 12, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
